Z||000000||briguy||06-11-2001||08:37 PM||||hi guys......and girls,<BR>I just joined and need your help. My headlight dash switch and dimmer switch back lighting has quit working. I took it apart but cant find out how that thing is lighted. Looked in my tech manual but it was no help at all. Can anybody give me a clue..........or just the answer on how to fix it ? Can't post a pic yet but mines an 85 GT and boy do I love that car ! ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Rodrv6||06-11-2001||08:54 PM||||The headlight switch and the dash dimmer switch don't have any backlighting.  The only switches that have that are the decklid release and the buttons on the heater/air conditioner control panel.  The rear window defrost may have it--I don't have that option on mine.<P>------------------<BR>Rod Schneider, Woodstock, Ga.  84 SE, 330,000 miles and counting, 88 GT, not nearly as many miles :)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Ken Wittlief||06-12-2001||01:56 PM||||hey I never though of that - the headlight switch is an interesting problem in human-interface design.<P>Ill bet the engineers went around and around on that one.<P> When the dash is all lit up, the headlight switch is already on, so you dont need to know where it is<P>  and if its on, and its dark out, you dont want to turn it off or you will wreck your car<P>  so what you would need is a headlight switch backlight that is on when the headlights are off, and it dark, and you are in the car, but not always...<P>  I think some newer cars have lights on the ignition switch that stay on for a minute after you open the door.<P>  but it really doesnt make any sense to light the headlight switch, does it.<P>  "turn the headlights on so I can find the headlight switch..." I never thought of that before - its a paradox wrapped in an enigma.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Mr.Frosty||06-12-2001||02:30 PM||||More like "Heavy sarcasm wrapped in a twinkie"<P>------------------<BR>85 GT Turbo intercooled||||reg||12
Z||000004||Ken Wittlief||06-12-2001||03:07 PM||||no seriously, simple things like that end up being on the final exams in engineering design classes. <P> another one is designing a signaling system so trains from two directions can pass through a tunnel with one track - its not that simple<P>  or like the stupid answering machines we had at my last office. You had to call a number to see if you have any messages. But if anyone calls while you are calling to see if you have any messages, then they have to leave a message - so while you are checking, you could get one, so you have to check again<P>  kinda like when you are expecting a call and you pick up the phone to see if its working - did they just call while you had the phone off the hook, and now you missed it?<P>   A lighted headlight switch is an interesting engineering design problem. sorry if my last post sounded sarcastic.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Carrolles||06-12-2001||04:43 PM||||I was designing a laboratory building for a plant and the OSHA inspector insisted that I put braille lables on every light switch.<P>Go figure.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ken Wittlief||06-12-2001||04:56 PM||||yeah, blind people like to turn the lights off on everybody when they get frustrated: "SEE! How do you like it!"<P>  I worked in a building where they put motion sensors in the mens room. If you used one of the stalls and closed its door, then the motion sensor couldnt see you anymore, and after 3 minutes it would turn the lights off and leave you stranded in there in the dark. You had to open the stall door to get the lights to go back on.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Ken Wittlief||06-12-2001||04:59 PM||||they had them in the conference rooms too, with a ten minute delay.<P> one time we had a meeting with about 15 people in the room, and the guy that was doing all the talking was sitting down.<P>  he was so boring he was putting us all to sleep, and right in the middle of a sentace the lights went off - nobody had moved for 10 minutes - it was hilarious!||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||06-12-2001||10:45 PM||||I have no trouble finding my headlite switch. But just to be different and look cool in my kit, I took out the stock switches, mounted led lit rocker switches in the bezel and thats it. I mounted 2 switches above each other and they fit in perfect. one is for headlites, one is for park/tail lites. cool thing is i can leave my headlites on and everything else off for gettaways. lol. I never forget and leave my lites on either, they glow rite in my face if i do, even in brite sunshine.||||reg||1
